g · A recipe","blocks":[{"type":"text","title":"Easy Cancel-Proof Pizza","paras":["You **don’t have to** make the dough: buy it ready. But you **mustn’t** forget the oven: it **must** be hot. If guests **cancel**, you **don’t have to** worry — the pizza keeps well.","You **mustn’t** open the oven door too often. And remember: you **don’t have to** cut it perfectly!"],"kicker":"RECIPE","by":"Home cook","gloss":[["dough","massa"],["guest","convidado"],["keep well","conservar bem"],["perfectly","perfeitamente"]]}]},{"tag":"Compreensão","title":"Did you understand?","blocks":[{"type":"tfng","title":"","items":[{"q":"You don’t have to make the dough.","ans":"T","why":"don’t have to."},{"q":"You mustn’t forget the oven.","ans":"T","why":"mustn’t forget."},{"q":"You must cut it perfectly.","ans":"F","why":"don’t have to."}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Vocabulary in context","items":[{"q":"“dough” = ?","opts":["massa","pasta","ponto"],"ans":0,"why":"dough."},{"q":"“cancel” = ?","opts":["cancelar","calcular","carregar"],"ans":0,"why":"cancel."}]}]},{"tag":"Gramática","title":"don’t have to × mustn’t","blocks":[{"type":"table","head":["Forma","Sentido","Exemplo"],"rows":[["**don’t have to**","não é preciso","**You don’t have to make the dough.**"],["**mustn’t**","é proibido","**You mustn’t forget the oven.**"],["**must**","é obrigatório","**The oven must be hot.**"]],"cap":"don’t have to × mustn’t"},{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Regra","body":"Armadilha: *don’t have to* ≠ *mustn’t*. Pergunta: *Do I have to…?* (não *Must I…?* no uso comum)."},{"type":"box","kind":"warn","t":"Cuidado","body":"*mustn’t* /ˈmʌsənt/ — o t final é fraco."}]},{"tag":"Prática","title":"Practice","blocks":[{"type":"gap","title":"Complete the sentences","bank":null,"items":[{"s":"You ___ make the dough. (don’t have to)","a":"don’t have to","why":"não é preciso."},{"s":"You ___ forget the oven. (mustn’t)","a":"mustn’t","why":"proibido."},{"s":"The oven ___ be hot. (must)","a":"must","why":"obrigatório."},{"s":"If guests ___ , don’t worry. (cancel)","a":"cancel","why":"cancel."}]},{"type":"match","title":"Match the word to its meaning","pairs":[["dough","massa"],["topping","cobertura"],["oven","forno"],["guest","convidado"],["cancel","cancelar"]]},{"type":"order","title":"Put the words in order","items":[{"words":["oven","Can","I","open","the"],"ans":"Can I open the oven","pt":"Posso abrir o forno?"},{"words":["I","have","to","make","the","dough","Do"],"ans":"Do I have to make the dough","pt":"Preciso fazer a massa?"}]}]},{"tag":"Vocabulário","title":"Words and expressions","blocks":[{"type":"vocab","items":[{"w":"cancel","pos":"word","pt":"cancelar","ex":"Cancel the order.","expt":"Cancele o pedido."},{"w":"ready-made","pos":"word","pt":"pronto","ex":"Ready-made dough.","expt":"Massa pronta."},{"w":"perfectly","pos":"word","pt":"perfeitamente","ex":"Cut it perfectly.","expt":"Corte perfeitamente."},{"w":"pizza dough","pos":"word","pt":"pizza dough","ex":"massa de pizza","expt":"Pizza dough."},{"w":"pizza sauce","pos":"word","pt":"pizza sauce","ex":"molho de pizza","expt":"Pizza sauce."},{"w":"oven rack","pos":"word","pt":"oven rack","ex":"grade do forno","expt":"Oven rack."},{"w":"hot oven","pos":"word","pt":"hot oven","ex":"forno quente","expt":"Hot oven."},{"w":"cheese topping","pos":"word","pt":"cheese topping","ex":"cobertura de queijo","expt":"Cheese topping."},{"w":"ready dough","pos":"word","pt":"ready dough","ex":"massa pronta","expt":"Ready dough."},{"w":"cooking time","pos":"word","pt":"cooking time","ex":"tempo de preparo","expt":"Cooking time."},{"w":"pizza stone","pos":"word","pt":"pizza stone","ex":"pedra de pizza","expt":"Pizza stone."},{"w":"tomato sauce","pos":"word","pt":"tomato sauce","ex":"molho de tomate","expt":"Tomato sauce."},{"w":"thin slice","pos":"word","pt":"thin slice","ex":"fatia fina","expt":"Thin slice."},{"w":"dinner guests","pos":"word","pt":"dinner guests","ex":"convidados do jantar","expt":"Dinner guests."},{"w":"pizza night","pos":"word","pt":"pizza night","ex":"noite de pizza","expt":"Pizza night."},{"w":"table setting","pos":"word","pt":"table setting","ex":"mesa posta","expt":"Table setting."}]},{"type":"box","kind":"culture","t":"Expressões desta aula","body":["**Do I have to make the dough?** — Preciso fazer a massa?","**No, you don’t have to. Buy it.** — Não precisa. Compre.","**Can I open the oven?** — Posso abrir o forno?","**It was a nightmare.** — Foi um pesadelo.","**It was nothing special.** — Não foi nada de especial.","**It was out of this world.** — Foi sensacional.","**It cost me a fortune.** — Me custou uma fortuna."]}]},{"tag":"Verbos","title":"Verbs in focus","blocks":[{"type":"verbs","items":[{"v":"cancel","pt":"cancelar","forms":[["I / you / we / they cancel","I cancel the order."],["he / she / it cancels","She cancels the plan."]]}]}]},{"tag":"Escuta e diálogo","title":"In the kitchen","blocks":[{"type":"dialog","title":"In the kitchen","lines":[["Ana","Do I have to make the dough?","Preciso fazer a massa?"],["Leo","No, you don’t have to. Buy it.","Não precisa. Compre."],["Ana","Can I open the oven?","Posso abrir o forno?"],["Leo","You mustn’t open it too often.","Você não deve abrir com frequência."]]},{"type":"pron","title":"Pronúncia: Plural e 3ª pessoa /s/ /z/ /ɪz/","items":[{"label":"Plural e 3ª pessoa /s/ /z/ /ɪz/","note":"Pratique em voz alta.","words":[]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"Say what you don’t have to do on Sunday.","pt":"Diga.","model":"I don’t have to work on Sunday."},{"q":"Say a prohibition with mustn’t.","pt":"Diga.","model":"You mustn’t park here."},{"q":"Ask: Do I have to…?","pt":"Pergunte.","model":"Do I have to pay?"}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write 5 sentences with don’t have to / mustn’t / must.","model":"You don’t have to make the dough. You mustn’t forget the oven. The oven must be hot. If guests cancel, don’t worry. You mustn’t open the door often.","checklist":["Usei **don’t have to**","Usei **mustn’t**","Usei **must**"],"words":"5 frases"}]},{"tag":"Revisão e exame","title":"Review · Exam strategy · Teacher’s note","blocks":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Check yourself","items":[{"q":"What does “dough” mean?","opts":["cobertura","convidado","massa"],"ans":2,"why":"**dough** = massa."},{"q":"What does “topping” mean?","opts":["cobertura","forno","cancelar"],"ans":0,"why":"**topping** = cobertura."},{"q":"What does “oven” mean?","opts":["convidado","forno","pronto"],"ans":1,"why":"**oven** = forno."},{"q":"What does “guest” mean?","opts":["cancelar","porta","convidado"],"ans":2,"why":"**guest** = convidado."}]},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Estratégia para as provas","body":["Treine esta habilidade com o formato de tarefas curtas das provas (TOEFL/IELTS).","Leia o enunciado primeiro e procure as palavras-chave."]},{"type":"box","kind":"teach","t":"Nota para o futuro professor","body":["Use exemplos reais da vida dos alunos e peça frases próprias.","Corrija o erro mais frequente da aula em grupo, sem expor o aluno.","Retome o conteúdo na aula seguinte com um exercício curto."]}]}]}